From 2ffe97a411815271b66288e740305caaa63e6a9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nmburgan <13688219+nmburgan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 03:22:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Read event data hashes with the stringifying converter

Event#to_data_hash writes event data with ToStringifiedConverter, while
#initialize_from_hash read it back with FromDataConverter. Read with the
same stringifying converter so a deserialized event contains only plain data
and reconstructs no rich values. A rich-typed value written by a Puppet 5
agent is no longer reconstructed into an object. Its tagged hash arrives
with the reserved keys renamed instead.

Signed-off-by: nmburgan <13688219+nmburgan@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 lib/puppet/transaction/event.rb | 7 +++----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/puppet/transaction/event.rb b/lib/puppet/transaction/event.rb
index 7893db862b..0ab95a4193 100644
--- a/lib/puppet/transaction/event.rb
+++ b/lib/puppet/transaction/event.rb
@@ -68,10 +68,9 @@ class Puppet::Transaction::Event
   alias == eql?
 
   def initialize_from_hash(data)
-    data = Puppet::Pops::Serialization::FromDataConverter.convert(data, {
-                                                                    :allow_unresolved => true,
-                                                                    :loader => Puppet::Pops::Loaders.static_loader
-                                                                  })
+    # Read with the stringifying converter, the same one #to_data_hash writes with.
+    # Event values contain no rich data downstream, so there is nothing to reconstruct.
+    data = Puppet::Pops::Serialization::ToStringifiedConverter.convert(data, :message_prefix => 'Event')
     @audited = data['audited']
     @property = data['property']
     @previous_value = data['previous_value']
